{{Quote|Their advantage: superior numbers. My advantage: superior intelligence!|Brainstorm, analyzing the [[Vengers]].<ref name="TV" />}}
Brainstorm's cranium holds an immense brain, giving him super-massive intelligence that is too high to be measured on a [[Human (Classic)|human]] scale.{{Refn|[[:File:Brainstorm Alien Creation Card.png]]|group = Bandai|name = Bandai2}} Technically speaking, his IQ is shown to be 10^30, or one nonillion.<ref name="TV" /> He can solve very difficult calculations mentally in roughly seconds, and can visualize equations and trajectories of objects as if they're actually there.<ref name="GfT">''[[Greetings From Techadon]]''</ref> He can even determine the mechanical values and physical properties of things by simply looking at them. In combat, Brainstorm is shown to be able to perfectly intuit and predict the mindsets, mannerisms, weaknesses, and attacks of his enemies; as well as being able to use his environment and any ordinary objects within it to win the fight with the minimal amount of moves. After defeating the [[Vengers]], Brainstorm even got the idea for Ben to briefly quit being a superhero, calculating that their individual egos would turn them against each other in a matter of months once he removed himself from the picture; though he made one miscalculation (they only lasted a few hours).<ref name="TV" />

Brainstorm can produce and manipulate electricity{{Refn|Brainstorm's electricity was originally yellow in '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]''' and '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' before being recolored green in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]'''. Meanwhile, alternate versions of Brainstorm are shown generating electricity in different colors. For example, Negative Brainstorm's electricity is colored red.<ref name="AFOB" />|group=note}} by both thinking hard enough{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/3/38/AF_Mini_Bible.pdf Alien Force Series Mini Bible]|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible}}  and opening the exoskeleton plates on his skull. This electrical energy can be used in a variety of ways, such as electrocuting or launching enemies and disabling or destroying machinery. He can also charge up his electrical energy to produce a concentrated beam of electricity strong enough to blast [[Ship]] out of the air.<ref name="Pier" /> Additionally, he can control the voltage of his electrokinetic attacks.<ref name="TV" /> Brainstorm can also generate constructs with his electricity, as shown when [[Ultimate Kevin]] created a shield made of electricity to block [[Argit]]'s quills.<ref name="TEoME">''[[The Enemy of My Enemy]]''</ref>

Brainstorm is capable of conducting his electricity throughout his body, as shown when [[Albedo|Negative]] Brainstorm did so through his closed skull plates to get [[Astrodactyl]] off of him,<ref name="AFOB">''[[A Fistful of Brains]]''</ref> and when Brainstorm fired electricity from out of his pincers.<ref name="EotB" />

Brainstorm can use his electrokinesis to telekinetically move objects, the size and mass of which ranging from trains to living beings without damaging or hurting them.<ref name="Inferno">''[[Inferno]]''</ref> Brainstorm can also control machinery and other technology with his electricity, giving him a form of technokinesis.<ref name="EfA" />

Brainstorm can generate pulses from his brain to block attacks and knock away enemies,<ref name="EotB">''[[Eye of the Beholder]]''</ref> generate protective force fields powerful enough to topple an [[Ultimate Arburian Pelarota]],<ref>''[[The Ultimate Sacrifice]]''</ref> and even produce electrical storms.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = Bandai1}}

Brainstorm can levitate several stories above the ground.<ref name="Inferno" /><ref name="EotB" />

Brainstorm is strong enough to pin opponents against walls,<ref name="TV" /> rip off an [[Arachnachimp (Classic)|Arachnachimp]]'s webs,<ref name="VoVP2" /> or crush a refrigerator with his pinchers.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = Bandai2}} His pincers are also sharp enough to stab through metal.<ref name="TV" />

Despite having a soft body,{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = Bandai1}} Brainstorm is very durable thanks to his shell,<ref name="TV" /> which can withstand laser and gun fire.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = Bandai2}} His exoskeleton can also act like a protective coat, which can resist the cold temperatures of places such as mountains.<ref name="EfA">''[[Escape From Aggregor]]''</ref>

Brainstorm is very agile and can perform acrobatics such as somersaults and forward rolls.<ref>''[[Singlehanded]]''</ref>

Brainstorm is capable of breathing underwater thanks to his gills, which he has to keep moist when he is on land.{{Refn|[[:File:Brainstorm Has Gills.PNG]]|group = DM}}

Brainstorm can scale walls<ref name="TV" /> and walk on an Arachnachimp's webs.<ref name="VoVP2" />

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
Fused (416).png|Ineffective Electrokinesis
GCBC (424).png|Concentration Interruption
EfA (54).png|Slippery Surfaces
</gallery>
Brainstorm's electric attacks are ineffective against weapons that were made specifically for electrokinetic aliens, such as the [[Shock Staff]].<ref>''[[Fused]]''</ref>

If Brainstorm's shell is closed when releasing electricity, it will shock and injure his brain, as demonstrated with [[Dr. Psychobos]].<ref name="TFoW2" />

Because Brainstorm needs to concentrate to use his electrokinesis,{{Refn|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible}} things that causes him headaches, such as the sonic screams of a [[Sonorosian]], can impair him.<ref>''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]''</ref>

Being a [[Cerebrocrustacean]], Brainstorm is at a massive disadvantage against a [[Vicetopus|Vicetopus]] due to their large size and resistance to electricity.<ref>''[[Showdown: Part 1]]''</ref>

Brainstorm has difficulty walking on slippery surfaces, such as snow and ice.<ref name="EfA" />

==History==
===Alien Force===
*Brainstorm first appeared in ''[[Pier Pressure]]'', where he defeated [[Ship]] and protected [[Julie Yamamoto|Julie]] from him.
**The same scene reoccurred on TV in ''[[Fame]]''.
*In ''[[What Are Little Girls Made Of?]]'', Brainstorm defeated [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] in a play-fight.
*In ''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]'', Brainstorm defeated [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Big Chill (Classic)|Big Chill]], but was defeated himself by Negative [[Echo Echo]], so he switched into [[Jetray (Classic)|Jetray]].
*In ''[[Voided]]'', Brainstorm saved [[Manny Armstrong|Manny]] from some [[Null Guardian]] and battled [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|D'Void]] before retreating with Manny and [[Helen Wheels|Helen]]. Later, Brainstorm was defeated by D'Void.
*In ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 2]]'', Brainstorm piloted Ship in "Battle Mode" to reach [[Augstaka]], during which he and [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]] had some banter.
*In ''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]'', Brainstorm fought and recaptured the escaped [[Spidermonkey (Classic)|Spidermonkey]].
*In ''[[Inferno]]'', Brainstorm built a pen for some [[Pyroxovore]]s out of a train and some railway tracks.
*In ''[[Singlehanded]]'', Brainstorm battled [[Sunder]] before switching into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]].

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]'', Brainstorm was scanned by [[Oliver Thompson]] for the [[Stalker]] off-screen.
*In ''[[Escape From Aggregor]]'', Brainstorm took control of a [[Yeti]], told it to attack [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]], and then freed it before capturing the latter.
*In ''[[Fused]]'', Brainstorm was defeated and nearly killed by [[Aggregor]], but was saved by [[Ra'ad]].
*In ''[[Eye of the Beholder]]'', Brainstorm defeated [[Strabismus]] and freed [[Baz-L]], but accidentally awoke the [[Sentinels of Monawk]] in the process.
*In ''[[Greetings From Techadon]]'', Brainstorm got a hole in one in golf using his "mental calculations." He then switched into [[Goop (Classic)|Goop]] to fight a [[Techadon Robot]].
*In ''[[The Ultimate Sacrifice]]'', Brainstorm defeated [[Sentient Ultimate Cannonbolt]] before switching into [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]].
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Brainstorm appeared as one of the many aliens when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was explaining his story to [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]].
*In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', [[Albedo|Negative]] Brainstorm figured out that [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] somehow broke free from the [[Cassiopeian Dream Eater]] in a dream.

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Malefactor]]'', a kid failed to dunk Brainstorm before the latter was successfully dunked by another kid.
*In ''[[A Fistful of Brains]]'', [[Albedo|Negative]] Brainstorm briefly fought [[Astrodactyl]] until they both reverted.
*In ''[[The Vengers]]'', Brainstorm defeated the [[Vengers]] and soon afterwards formulated a plan which comprised their fellowship.
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Brainstorm appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

===[[Original Future Timeline|Original Future]]=== 
*Prior to ''[[Ken 10]]'', Brainstorm was among the intelligent aliens used by [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]] to create an [[Omnitrix (Ken's Replica)|Omnitrix]] for his [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|son]]'s 10 birthday.{{Refn|[[:File:Aliens Ben 10,000 Used to Create Ken's Omnitrix.png]]|group = pop-up|name = pop-up}}<ref name="K10">''[[Ken 10]]''</ref>

