==Etymology==
Brainstorm's name comes from the word "brainstorm", which means a spontaneous group discussion to create new ideas and solve problems. It references how he always creates new ideas and solves problems with his IQ. It also refers to the electrical powers in his brain, as electricity is usually produced from "storm" clouds.

==Trivia==
*In '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]''' and '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''', Brainstorm spoke with a [[Wikipedia:United Kingdom|British]] accent. As of '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', Brainstorm speaks with an [[Wikipedia:Austria|Austrian]] accent.
**The reason Brainstorm has a British accent in '''Alien Force''' and '''Ultimate Alien''' is because the British are stereotyped as being smart and royal.
**Brainstorm's accent in '''Omniverse''' is based on that of [[Wikipedia:Ludwig Von Drake|Ludwig Von Drake]],{{Refn|[[:File:Brainstorm OV Accent.png]]|group = DJW}} who Corey Burton had voiced in numerous Disney projects.
** Burton would exaggerate the accent and use a higher pitch as Negative Brainstorm in '''Omniverse'''.
*Brainstorm's mouth does not move except to show emotion.
**In ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 2]]'', his mouth opened when he accidentally vomited on [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]].
*Brainstorm was originally one of two aliens featured in '''Ultimate Alien''' who generate yellow electricity; the other being [[Shocksquatch]].
*Official sources have provided different explanations on how Brainstorm speaks:
**[[Dwayne McDuffie]] stated that he electrostatically vibrates gaseous or liquid mediums.{{Refn|[[:File:DM Explanation on How Brainstorm Speaks.png]]|group = DM}}
**[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] stated that his thoughts are projected mentally.{{Refn|[[:File:Cerebrocrustacean Telepathy and Filter Feeders.png]]|group = DJW}} 
**Brainstorm's Alien Creation card tangentially called it a "secret mind link".{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = Bandai2}}
*Brainstorm is one of five aliens featured in '''Omniverse''' who generate green electricity; the others being [[Upgrade (Classic)|Upgrade]], [[Buzzshock (Classic)|Buzzshock]], [[Frankenstrike]], and [[Nanomech]].
*Brainstorm was among the three intelligent aliens used by [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]] to create [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken]]'s [[Omnitrix (Ken's Replica)|Omnitrix]]. The others are [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]] and [[Frankenstrike]].{{Refn|group = pop-up|name = pop-up}}<ref name="K10" />
**This has been slightly retconned in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', as Ben does not become any smarter as Frankenstrike.{{Refn|[[:File:Transylians Enhanced Intelligence Retconned.png]]|group = DJW}}
*[[Madison (Omniverse)|Madison]] likes Brainstorm better than [[Rath (Classic)|Rath]].<ref name = "MHR"/>
*Unlike [[Servantis]], Brainstorm is unable to tamper with the thoughts and memories of other beings.{{Refn|[[:File:Only Servantis can Alter Memories.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Brainstorm had concept art drawn by [[Eric Canete]],{{Refn|[[:File:Eric Canete Designed Brainstorm Concepts.png]]|group = EC}} whereas his final design was created by [[Glenn Wong]], with color styling by Chris Hooten.{{Refn|https://archive.is/QjUy1|group = GW}}
*Brainstorm was originally not supposed to appear in:
**''[[Escape From Aggregor]]'', with his role taken by [[Ultimate Humungousaur]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/6/60/EFA_Script_Outline.pdf ''Escape From Aggregor'' Script Outline]|group = outline}}
**The dream in ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/d/d4/Night_of_the_Living_Nightmare_Script_First_Draft.pdf ''Night of the Living Nightmare'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = first}}
*Brainstorm was originally supposed to appear in:
**''[[It's Not Easy Being Gwen]]'' to reverse the effects of [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]]'s transmodulator ray.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/b/bf/INEBG_Script_Outline.pdf ''It's Not Easy Being Gwen'' Script Outline]|group = outline}}
**''[[Inspector 13]]'', used by [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/f/f1/Inspector_13_Script_DRAFT-1.pdf ''Inspector 13'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = script}}
*In Derrick's opinion, Brainstorm is a brain alien with some minorly electric side powers, hence why he did not appear in ''[[Max's Monster]]'' alongside the rest of Ben's electric-based aliens.{{Refn|[[:File:Brainstorm Not In Max's Monster Reason.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Brainstorm was considered to appear in the [[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|Reboot]] but did not make the cut as an electric alien for [[Ben Tennyson (Reboot)|Ben]] because [[Shock Rock]] was created for plot purposes.{{Refn|[[:File:Shock Rock's Purpose.png]]|group = DR}}
*In May 2018, a recording of the [[Toy Line/4" Collection#Defenders|Ultimate Omnitrix]] toy became a viral auditory illusion, asking whether viewers heard {{W|Yanny or Laurel#Brainstorm_/_green_needle|the phrase "Green needle" or the name "Brainstorm"}} upon Brainstorm's hologram accessory being latched onto the toy.

